air/OS (Haiku arm64): Mesa 26.2.4's Turnip (freedreno Vulkan, "msm" kernel
interface) on the native "adreno" kernel driver (/dev/graphics/adreno/0,
Radxa Dragon Q8B, SC8280XP Adreno 690).

The kernel takes Linux's drm.h / msm_drm.h structures unchanged behind op
codes ADRENO_HAIKU_OP(nr) (headers/private/graphics/adreno/adreno_haiku.h in
the air/OS tree, put on the include path by build.sh, not copied). All
changes are #ifdef __HAIKU__ except fd_path's size.

  include/drm-uapi/drm.h            BSD ioctl encoding from <bsd/sys/ioccom.h>
  include/xf86drm.h                 libdrm stand-in (Haiku only, #include_next
                                    elsewhere), the PowerVR one's
                                    (tools/cubie-a7s/mesa) on ADRENO_HAIKU_OP:
                                    drmIoctl, drmCommand*, version, caps,
                                    syncobjs, drmDevice types
  include/vk_haiku_scanout.h        the private scanout import (from the
                                    PowerVR patch), which zink's direct
                                    present (mesa-haiku-gl.patch) includes;
                                    Turnip does not take it yet
  src/util/libdrm.h                 that stand-in rather than the no-op shim
  src/util/u_sync_provider_haiku.c  the Vulkan runtime's syncobj provider on
  src/util/u_sync_provider.h          those wrappers (from the PowerVR patch)
  src/util/meson.build
  src/vulkan/runtime/meson.build    build vk_drm_syncobj.c without libdrm
  ir3_disk_cache.c                  no build-id notes on Haiku: no ir3 disk
                                    cache (the shader cache is off anyway)
  tu_knl.cc                         no device list: HAIKU_ADRENO_DEVICE or
                                    /dev/graphics/adreno/0 as the only, render
                                    only, platform device; no major()/minor();
                                    unmapping deletes the clone's area
  tu_knl_drm_msm.cc                 buffers are mapped with
                                    ADRENO_HAIKU_NR_MAP_BO (no mmap of
                                    devices), placed or not, and unmapped with
                                    delete_area()
  tu_device.h                       fd_path 64 bytes: "/dev/graphics/adreno/0"
                                    does not fit 20

